.TH GETHOSTNAME 2X 3/17/82
.UC 4.1a Provisional
.SH NAME
gethostname \- get name of current host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "gethostname(hostname, sizeof (hostname))"
.br
.B "char hostname[];"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Gethostname
returns the standard host name for the current processor, as set by
.IR sethostname (2x)
and defined in
.IR rhost (3x).
The name is null-terminated.
.SH SEE ALSO
sethostname(2x)
.SH BUGS
